{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Oil for the lamp.</b> Pure olive oil, to kindle the lamp continually." "<b>Spices for the anointing oil.</b> Which was made to anoint the vessels of the Tabernacle and the Tabernacle, to sanctify them — and it required spices for this, as is explained in כִּי תִשָּׂא." "<b>And for the incense of spices.</b> Which they would burn every evening and morning, as is explained in וְאַתָּה תְּצַוֶּה — and קְטֹרֶת is a term for raising smoke and sending up smoke."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:22.615911617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}